   "date": "2013-05-16",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The bill amends the Aviation Transport Security Act 2004 to allow the government to quickly prohibit or restrict inbound air cargo via disallowable instruments, with strict liability penalties of $34,000 for aircraft operators and $17,000 for other industry participants, following the 2010 Yemen incident where explosives were hidden in printers."
